# pyenv
#   For local projects, check in .python-version if needed.

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if having platform-specific dependencies or dependencies
#   having no cross-platform support, this file may be included.
# Pipfile.lock

# UV
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include uv.lock in version control.
#   This is especially recommended for libraries.
# uv.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
# poetry.lock
# poetry.toml

# pdm
#   pdm recommends including project-wide configuration in version control.
#   https://pdm-project.org/en/latest/usage/project/#commit-your-pdm-lock-file-to-version-control
# pdm.lock
# pdm.toml
.pdm-python
.pdm-build/

# pixi
#   Pixi creates a virtual environment in the .pixi directory, just like venv module creates a virtual environment.
#   It is recommended not to include the .pixi directory in version control.
# pixi.lock
.pixi

# PEP 582; used by github.com/David-OConnor/pyflow and others
